WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:05.580
Improving lives,...

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.420
...increasing connectivity across the world.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.840
That's the great promise
 offered by data-driven technology.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.520
[Protests]

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:21.840
But in China, it also promises
 greater state control and abuse of power.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.660
[Protests]

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:37.880
This is the next groundbreaking development
 in data driven technology:...

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:40.740
...facial recognition.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:45.900
And in China
 you can already withdraw cash,...

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.860
...check-in at airports,...

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:53.760
...and pay for goods,
 using just your face.

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:59.340
The country is the world's leader
 in the use of this emerging technology.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:03.360
And China's many
 artificial intelligence startups...

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:06.960
...are determined
 to keep it that way in the future.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:10.940
Companies like YITU.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:16.330
We're pioneering...

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:18.960
...Artificial Intelligence research and innovation,...

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:23.920
...in the hope of creating
 a safer, faster, and healthier world.

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:28.500
[Chinese]

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:32.680
YITU is creating the building blocks
 for a smart city of the future,...

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:36.260
...where facial recognition
 is part of everyday life.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:40.700
This could even extend to detecting
 what people are thinking.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:44.240
Facial recognition:
 they can read people's emotions,...

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:51.280
...and we are actually now working
 on these innovative demonstrations and technology.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:57.100
But the Chinese government has plans
 to use this new biometric technology...

00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:00.040
...to cement its authoritarian rule.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:05.920
The country has ambitious plans
 to develop a vast national surveillance system,...

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:08.460
...based on facial recognition.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.980
It'll be used to monitor
 its 1.4 billion citizens...

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:14.780
...in unprecedented ways.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:20.420
With the capability of tracking everything,
 from their emotions...   to their sexuality.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:26.120
The primary means
 will be a vast network of CCTV cameras.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:29.080
A 170 million are already in place,...

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:34.780
...and an estimated 400 million new ones
 will be installed over the next three years.

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:40.320
The authorities insist this program
 will allow them to improve security for citizens,...

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:44.340
...and if you have nothing to hide,
 you have nothing to fear.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.800
But not everyone is convinced.

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:53.400
[Chinese]

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:57.040
Hongshen Kwai is a former magazine editor.

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:59.360
He was ousted by the government.

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:02.560
He feels like he's under constant surveillance.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:14.460
[Chinese]

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:23.260
Already the authorities are using facial recognition
 to name and shame citizens.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:27.680
Even for minor offenses,
 like jaywalking.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:31.300
In Beijing,...

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.320
...they're using the technology
 to prevent people...

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:36.980
...stealing rolls of loo paper
 from public toilets.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:42.420
And across China, police officers
 are now trialing sunglasses and body cameras,...

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:45.680
...loaded with facial and gesture
 recognition technology.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:50.480
It's helping them to identify
 wanted suspects in real-time.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:53.300
What worries some people here...

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:59.600
...is that, as the technology develops,
 so too does the capacity for it to be abused.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:18.280
[Chinese]

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:23.580
Some of those most at risk
 in this hyper-surveillance future...

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:26.520
...are the ethnic minorities in China.

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:31.880
In Xinjiang province, the Chinese government
 is wary of the separatist threat...

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:35.080
...posed by the Muslim Uyghur population.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.060
According to local NGOs,...

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:40.520
...an estimated 1 million Uyghurs...

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:44.080
...are being detained indefinitely
 in secretive internment camps,...

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:46.880
...where some are being subject to abuse.

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:53.120
It's been called the largest mass incarceration
 of a minority population in the world today.

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:59.820
The authorities are using facial recognition cameras
 to scan people's faces before they enter markets.

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:06.980
The system alerts authorities if targeted individuals stray 300 meters beyond their home.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:12.120
In the future, the government plans
 to aggregate even more data,...

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.360
...and build a predictive policing programme...

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:17.840
...that imposes even tighter controls here.

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:20.980
Without checks and balances,...

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:26.140
...China will keep finding new ways
 to violate the human rights of its citizens.

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:32.460
What's already happening in Xinjiang
 is a warning the rest of the world must heed.

